from s5_lib import *
# ---- 5 Databases
C(5,"Azure SQL authentication options?","**SQL authentication** (username and password in the database), **Microsoft Entra authentication** (users, groups, managed identities), or both. **Microsoft Entra-only authentication** turns SQL logins off. Set a **Microsoft Entra admin** on the server first.")
C(5,"Azure SQL firewall rules?","**Server-level IP rules** apply to every database on the logical server. **Database-level IP rules** apply to one database. **Virtual network rules** allow a subnet. 'Allow Azure services' opens the server to all of Azure, so prefer **private endpoints** and deny public access.")
C(5,"Transparent data encryption (TDE)?","Encrypts data files, logs and backups **at rest**, **on by default** for new databases. Uses a **service-managed key** or a **customer-managed key** in Key Vault. The app needs no changes.")
C(5,"Always Encrypted?","Encrypts chosen **columns in the client driver**, so the data stays encrypted in use and **database admins cannot see plaintext**. Keys stay with the client (for example in Key Vault).")
C(5,"Dynamic data masking and row-level security?","**Dynamic data masking** hides part of a column in query results for non-privileged users; the stored data is unchanged, so it is not encryption. **Row-level security** filters which rows a user can read or change.")
C(5,"Azure SQL auditing: destinations and scope?","Writes database events to a **storage account**, a **Log Analytics workspace** or **Event Hubs**, in any combination. A **server-level** policy covers all existing and new databases. If both server and database auditing are on, events are audited twice. Prefer server-level.")
C(5,"Auditing for SQL Managed Instance?","Configured **per instance** with T-SQL or the portal: create a server audit to a storage container (URL), or send audit events through **diagnostic settings** to Log Analytics or Event Hubs.")
C(5,"Defender for Databases?","Four plans: **Azure SQL databases**, **SQL servers on machines** (Azure, hybrid, multicloud), **open-source relational databases** (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB) and **Azure Cosmos DB**. Gives **threat alerts** (SQL injection, brute force, anomalous access) and, for SQL, **vulnerability assessment**.")
Q(5,"Security policy says no SQL logins may exist; only identities from the directory may connect to Azure SQL Database. What should you enable?","Microsoft Entra-only authentication",["Transparent data encryption","A server-level firewall rule","Dynamic data masking"],"Entra-only authentication disables SQL authentication for the server.")
Q(5,"Database administrators must not be able to read the credit card column, even when querying the table directly. What should you use?","Always Encrypted",["Transparent data encryption","Dynamic data masking","Row-level security"],"Always Encrypted keeps data encrypted from the client, so the server and DBAs never see plaintext. Masking can be bypassed by privileged users.")
Q(5,"You need one audit configuration that covers every database on a logical server, including databases created later, queryable with KQL. What should you configure?","Server-level auditing to a Log Analytics workspace",["Database-level auditing on each database to a storage account","Defender for SQL vulnerability assessment","A resource lock on the server"],"Server-level auditing applies to all databases, and Log Analytics supports KQL.")
Q(5,"Help desk staff should see only the last four digits of phone numbers in query results. The stored values must not change. What should you configure?","Dynamic data masking",["Always Encrypted","TDE with a customer-managed key","A database-level firewall rule"],"Masking changes what non-privileged users see, not what is stored.")
Q(5,"Which TWO are plans within Defender for Databases?",["Defender for Azure Cosmos DB","Defender for open-source relational databases"],["Defender for Key Vault","Defender for Resource Manager"],"The four database plans are Azure SQL, SQL servers on machines, open-source relational, and Cosmos DB.")
YN(5,["TDE protects data from a database administrator running SELECT statements.","A server-level firewall rule applies to all databases on the logical server.","Auditing can write to a storage account and a Log Analytics workspace at the same time."],[0,1,1],"TDE is encryption at rest only. Server rules cover all databases. Destinations can be combined.")
M(5,"Match each requirement to the SQL feature.",[("Encrypt files and backups at rest","Transparent data encryption"),("Hide column values from DBAs","Always Encrypted"),("Each sales rep sees only their own rows","Row-level security"),("Record who ran which statements","Auditing")],"At rest, in use, per row, on record.")
Q(5,"Defender for Cloud should alert on a possible SQL injection against SQL Server running on Azure VMs and on-premises servers. Which plan should you enable?","Defender for SQL servers on machines",["Defender for Azure SQL databases","Defender for Storage","Foundational CSPM"],"SQL Server on VMs and Arc-enabled servers is covered by the SQL servers on machines plan.")
D(5,"TDE","Always Encrypted","Encrypts in the client driver, so the server never sees plaintext.",1,"TDE works at rest on the server.")
D(5,"Dynamic data masking","Always Encrypted","Stored data is unchanged; only query results are obfuscated.",0,"Masking is presentation, not encryption.")
D(5,"Server-level firewall rule","Database-level firewall rule","Applies to a single database and travels with it.",1,"Database rules are stored in the database.")
D(5,"SQL auditing","Defender for SQL","Raises an alert for a suspected brute-force attack.",1,"Auditing records. Defender detects threats.")
# ---- 6 Network services
C(6,"NSG and ASG essentials for SC-500?","NSG rules: priority **100-4096**, lowest first, **first match wins**, stateful. Inbound is checked at the **subnet NSG then the NIC NSG**. **ASGs** let rules target roles (web, db) instead of IPs. Defaults end in **DenyAllInbound 65500**.")
C(6,"Azure Virtual Network Manager security admin rules?","Central rules applied to **network groups** of virtual networks, **evaluated before NSGs**. Actions: **Allow** (NSGs still evaluate after), **Deny** (stops; NSGs cannot override) and **Always Allow** (stops; NSGs cannot block). Priority **1-4096**.")
C(6,"AVNM deployment rules?","Rules live in **rule collections** inside a **security admin configuration**, which you **deploy** to regions. Only **one security admin configuration per region** (use several rule collections). Changes apply with a short delay (eventual consistency).")
C(6,"Securing Azure Virtual WAN?","Turn a virtual hub into a **secured virtual hub** by adding **Azure Firewall** (or a supported security partner) and manage it with **Azure Firewall Manager**. **Routing intent** sends internet and private traffic through the hub's firewall.")
C(6,"VPN security options?","**Site-to-site:** IPsec/IKE tunnels; use a **custom IPsec/IKE policy** for required algorithms. **Point-to-site:** authenticate with **Microsoft Entra ID** (supports Conditional Access and MFA), certificates or RADIUS, over OpenVPN or IKEv2.")
C(6,"Microsoft Entra Private Access?","Zero Trust network access to **private apps** without a VPN. Users run the **Global Secure Access client**; traffic reaches apps through **private network connectors** inside your network. Define apps with **Quick Access** or per-app segments and apply **Conditional Access** per app.")
C(6,"Private endpoint vs Private Link service?","**Private endpoint:** a NIC with a private IP in **your** VNet that connects to a PaaS resource (or to a Private Link service). **Private Link service:** **your own** service, behind a **Standard Load Balancer**, published so consumers connect with private endpoints; you approve connections.")
C(6,"Azure Firewall SKUs and rule types?","**Basic** (small sites, up to 250 Mbps; threat intelligence is **alert only**), **Standard** (threat intelligence **alert and deny**, DNS proxy, **web categories** by FQDN), **Premium** (adds **TLS inspection**, **IDPS**, full-path **URL filtering** and URL-based web categories). Rules: **DNAT**, **network**, **application**, managed in a **Firewall Policy**. Needs **AzureFirewallSubnet** and a UDR to steer traffic.")
C(6,"Network Watcher tools for effective rules?","**IP flow verify** (is this packet allowed, and by which rule), **NSG diagnostics** (also for ranges and service tags), **Effective security rules** (the combined rules on a NIC), **Next hop**, **Connection troubleshoot**. IP flow verify also checks **AVNM admin rules**.")
Q(6,"The central security team must block inbound SSH from the internet in every virtual network, and application teams must not be able to override it with their NSGs. What should you use?","An Azure Virtual Network Manager security admin rule with the Deny action",["An NSG rule with priority 100 in each subnet","An application security group","A user-defined route"],"Admin Deny rules are evaluated before NSGs and cannot be overridden by them.")
Q(6,"An AVNM security admin rule uses the Allow action for TCP 443. A subnet NSG denies TCP 443. What happens to the traffic?","It is denied by the NSG",["It is allowed, because admin rules win","It is allowed only for 60 seconds","It bypasses both rule sets"],"Allow passes the traffic on to NSG evaluation. Only Always Allow skips the NSG.")
Q(6,"Remote users need access to an internal web app without a VPN, with per-app Conditional Access. What should you deploy?","Microsoft Entra Private Access with a private network connector",["A site-to-site VPN","Azure Bastion","A service endpoint"],"Private Access is ZTNA for private apps through connectors and the Global Secure Access client.")
Q(6,"You must inspect outbound HTTPS traffic for malware and use signature-based intrusion detection and prevention. Which Azure Firewall SKU is required?","Premium",["Basic","Standard","Any SKU with DNS proxy"],"TLS inspection and IDPS are Premium features.")
Q(6,"A small branch firewall must block, not just log, traffic to known malicious IPs and domains, and allow web categories. What is the lowest Azure Firewall SKU that does this?","Standard",["Basic","Premium","None; use an NSG"],"Basic threat intelligence is alert only and has no web categories. Standard adds deny mode and FQDN-based web categories.")
Q(6,"Your team hosts an API on VMs behind a Standard Load Balancer and wants customers in other tenants to reach it privately from their own VNets. What should you create?","A Private Link service",["A service endpoint policy","A NAT gateway","A VNet peering to each customer"],"A Private Link service publishes your service so consumers create private endpoints to it.")
Q(6,"Which TWO authentication options are available for point-to-site VPN users?",["Microsoft Entra ID","Certificates"],["Storage account keys","SAS tokens"],"P2S supports Entra ID, certificate and RADIUS authentication.")
YN(6,["Only one security admin configuration can be deployed to a region per network manager.","An Always Allow admin rule can be blocked by a subnet NSG.","A secured virtual hub is a Virtual WAN hub with Azure Firewall or a security partner."],[1,0,1],"One config per region. Always Allow ends evaluation. Secured hubs add a firewall.")
M(6,"Match each Azure Firewall rule type to its job.",[("Publish an internal server on a public IP and port","DNAT rule"),("Allow by IP, port and protocol","Network rule"),("Allow outbound by FQDN","Application rule"),("Block known malicious IPs and domains","Threat intelligence")],"Translate, filter by L3/L4, filter by name, block by intel.")
Q(6,"A VM cannot receive traffic on port 8080. You need to know which rule denies it, including any Virtual Network Manager admin rules. Which tool should you use?","IP flow verify",["Next hop","Packet capture","Connection Monitor"],"IP flow verify returns allowed or denied and the rule, checking NSGs and AVNM admin rules.")
D(6,"Security admin rule","NSG rule","Evaluated first and set centrally across many VNets.",0,"Admin rules come before NSGs.")
D(6,"Allow (admin rule)","Always Allow (admin rule)","NSGs can still deny the traffic afterwards.",0,"Allow continues to NSG evaluation.")
D(6,"Private endpoint","Private Link service","Publishes your own load-balanced service to consumers.",1,"The service is the provider side.")
D(6,"Azure Firewall Standard","Azure Firewall Premium","Adds TLS inspection and IDPS.",1,"Premium features.")
D(6,"Entra Private Access","Point-to-site VPN","Per-app access through connectors, no network-level tunnel to the whole VNet.",0,"Private Access is Zero Trust network access.")
# ---- 7 Security for AI
C(7,"Finding overshared SharePoint data before Copilot uses it?","Purview **Data Security Posture Management** runs a **data risk assessment every week for the top 100 SharePoint sites by usage**, with no setup. Add **custom assessments** for chosen sites. Results show overshared and unlabeled sensitive content with fixes (labels, restricting access).")
C(7,"What does DSPM (for AI) give you?","Insight into **AI activity** (Copilot, agents, third-party AI sites), **one-click policies** (DLP, collection, insider risk), **data risk assessments** and compliance controls. Needs **Purview Audit** on; third-party AI sites also need **onboarded devices** and the **Purview browser extension**. Allow about 24 hours for data.")
C(7,"Real-time protection for Copilot Studio agents?","Agents already block prompt injection (UPIA and XPIA) by default. Adding **Microsoft Defender** (or another provider) as the **external threat detection** system makes the agent ask it **before every tool invocation**; the system answers **allow or block**. Only for agents with **generative orchestration**.")
C(7,"Microsoft Entra Agent ID: the objects?","**Agent identity blueprint** (template; holds the credentials), **agent identity** (one per agent instance; no credentials of its own), optional **agent's user account**. Each needs a **sponsor** (business accountability) and should have an **owner** (technical admin).")
C(7,"Conditional Access and governance for agent identities?","Conditional Access can target **agent identities** and use **agent risk** from ID Protection. Apply policy at the **blueprint** so all its agents inherit it; **disabling a blueprint blocks all its agents**. Govern access with **access packages**; expiry notices go to the sponsor.")
C(7,"Blast radius in Defender XDR?","In the **incident graph**, select a node (for example a compromised agent or identity) and choose **View blast radius**: a graph of paths from that node to **critical assets**, up to a few hops, scoped to your permissions. Needs onboarding to the **Microsoft Sentinel data lake**. Use it to judge impact, then disable the agent identity or its blueprint.")
C(7,"AI Gateway for Microsoft Foundry?","Backed by **Azure API Management**, enabled from the Foundry portal for a Foundry resource. It sits between clients and model deployments and enforces **tokens-per-minute limits and token quotas per project**, plus content safety, logging and semantic caching. Over the TPM limit returns **429**; over quota returns **403**.")
C(7,"Defender for AI Services?","A Defender for Cloud workload protection plan giving **threat protection for AI services**: alerts on jailbreaks, data leakage, credential theft and more, using **Prompt Shields** and threat intelligence, shown in Defender XDR. Optional **user prompt evidence** adds prompt snippets to alerts.")
C(7,"Foundry guardrails?","A **guardrail** is a set of **controls**; each has a **risk**, **intervention points** and an **action**. Points: **user input, tool call, tool response, output** (the two tool points are agents only). An **agent's guardrail fully overrides its model's**. Agents support **Annotate and block** only.")
C(7,"Data and AI security dashboard, and agents in the Microsoft 365 admin center?","**Defender for Cloud's Data and AI security dashboard** shows data and AI resources, protection coverage, top alerts, recommendations and attack paths; full use needs **Defender CSPM** with sensitive data discovery. The **Microsoft 365 admin center** is where you see, approve, block and assign **agents** for Microsoft 365 users.")
Q(7,"Before rolling out Microsoft 365 Copilot you must find SharePoint sites where sensitive files are shared too widely. What should you review first?","The default data risk assessment in Purview Data Security Posture Management",["The Defender for Cloud secure score","Azure Policy compliance","The Entra sign-in logs"],"DSPM assesses the top 100 SharePoint sites weekly for oversharing without any setup.")
Q(7,"A Copilot Studio agent must have each planned tool call checked by your security platform, which can block it before it runs. What should you configure?","External threat detection with Microsoft Defender as the provider",["A Foundry guardrail on the agent's model","A DLP policy on SharePoint","An NSG on the agent's subnet"],"The agent calls the threat detection endpoint before invoking each tool and follows its allow or block decision.")
Q(7,"All agents created from one blueprint must be blocked from signing in when their risk is high. Where should you apply the Conditional Access policy?","To the agent identity blueprint",["To each agent's sponsor","To the Global Administrator role","To the Foundry project"],"Policies applied at the blueprint are inherited by every agent identity created from it.")
Q(7,"Several teams share one Foundry resource. One project must not consume more than a set number of tokens per minute. What should you configure?","AI Gateway with a token limit for the project",["A guardrail with the Violence risk","Defender for AI Services","A budget alert"],"AI Gateway enforces TPM limits and token quotas at the project level.")
Q(7,"An agent in Foundry reads web pages through a tool. You must stop hidden instructions in a page from steering the agent. Which control fits?","An indirect attack control at the tool response intervention point",["A Hate control at user input","A token quota in AI Gateway","A protected material control at output"],"Indirect prompt injection arrives in tool responses, so scan and block there.")
Q(7,"Which TWO are needed for DSPM to report on users' activity with third-party AI websites?",["Devices onboarded to Microsoft Purview","The Microsoft Purview browser extension"],["An Azure Firewall Premium policy","A Foundry guardrail"],"Third-party AI site insights depend on onboarded devices and the browser extension.")
YN(7,["An agent identity stores its own client secret.","If an agent has its own guardrail, the model's guardrail still applies as well.","Defender for AI Services alerts appear in the Defender XDR portal."],[0,0,1],"Credentials sit on the blueprint. The agent guardrail fully overrides the model's. AI alerts integrate with Defender XDR.")
M(7,"Match each task to the tool.",[("Find overshared SharePoint content","Purview DSPM"),("Alert on a jailbreak attempt against a model","Defender for AI Services"),("Cap tokens per project","AI Gateway"),("Approve or block agents for Microsoft 365 users","Microsoft 365 admin center")],"Data posture, threat alerts, traffic control, admin control.")
Q(7,"Every agent identity must have someone accountable for deciding whether the agent is still needed. Which role is that?","Sponsor",["Owner","Blueprint principal","Agent user"],"The sponsor carries business accountability. The owner handles technical operations.")
D(7,"Sponsor","Owner","Business accountability for the agent's lifecycle.",0,"Owners are the technical admins.")
D(7,"Agent identity blueprint","Agent identity","Holds the credentials and acts as the kill switch for all its agents.",0,"Agent identities have no credentials of their own.")
D(7,"Tool call","Tool response","Where indirect prompt injection from external content is caught.",1,"Injected content comes back in the tool response.")
D(7,"Defender for AI Services","Purview DSPM","Raises security alerts on jailbreak and data leakage attempts at runtime.",0,"DSPM is about data posture and oversharing.")
D(7,"AI Gateway","Foundry guardrail","Limits tokens per minute for a project.",0,"Guardrails scan content. The gateway governs traffic.")
# ---- 8 Servers and VMs
C(8,"Disk encryption choices now?","**Server-side encryption** is always on (platform-managed or customer-managed keys through a **disk encryption set**). **Encryption at host** also covers temp disks and caches end to end: use it for new VMs. **Azure Disk Encryption** (BitLocker/DM-Crypt) **retires 15 Sept 2028**. **Confidential disk encryption** binds keys to the VM's TPM.")
C(8,"Azure Bastion planning?","Managed RDP/SSH over **TLS 443** with **no public IP on the VMs**. Needs **AzureBastionSubnet (/26 or larger)** and a Standard public IP. **Basic**, **Standard** (native client, file transfer, shareable links, scaling) and **Premium** (**session recording**, private-only). Reaches peered VNets.")
C(8,"Just-in-time (JIT) VM access?","Part of **Defender for Servers Plan 2**. Management ports stay **closed**; an authorized user **requests access** for a port, source IP and limited time, and Defender for Cloud adds a temporary allow rule to the **NSG or Azure Firewall**, then removes it.")
C(8,"Azure Arc for servers?","Installs the **Connected Machine agent** on on-premises, AWS or GCP servers so they appear as Azure resources. Then you can apply **Azure Policy and Machine Configuration**, **Defender for Servers**, Azure Monitor and Update Manager to them.")
C(8,"Defender for Servers Plan 1 vs Plan 2?","**P1:** Defender for Endpoint **EDR** plus core vulnerability management. **P2:** all of P1 plus **agentless scanning**, **JIT VM access**, **file integrity monitoring**, **premium Defender Vulnerability Management**, OS configuration assessment, regulatory compliance and a **500 MB per machine daily ingestion benefit**.")
C(8,"Onboarding hybrid and multicloud servers to Defender for Servers?","On-premises: onboard with **Azure Arc**. AWS and GCP: create a **connector** in Defender for Cloud, which onboards machines through Arc. The **Defender for Endpoint extension** is then installed automatically on supported machines.")
C(8,"Agentless scanning for VMs?","Takes **disk snapshots** and analyzes them out of band, with **no agent and no performance impact**. Finds **vulnerabilities, secrets and malware** and builds software inventory. Included with **Defender for Servers P2** or **Defender CSPM**; on by default with P2. You can exclude machines.")
C(8,"Trusted launch security features?","Security type **Trusted launch** (the default for Gen2 VMs) gives **Secure Boot** (only signed boot components), **vTPM** (measured boot and key storage) and **boot integrity monitoring** through attestation. Other security types: **Standard** and **Confidential VMs**.")
C(8,"Azure Machine Configuration?","Formerly Guest Configuration. **Audits or enforces settings inside the OS** (password policy, security baselines, installed software) through **Azure Policy**. Needs the **Machine Configuration extension** and a **system-assigned managed identity**; works on Azure VMs and **Arc-enabled servers**.")
Q(8,"RDP on production VMs must be closed by default and opened only on request, for a limited time and from the requester's IP. What should you enable?","Just-in-time VM access in Defender for Servers Plan 2",["Azure Bastion Developer SKU","A permanent NSG allow rule for the corporate range","Encryption at host"],"JIT keeps ports closed and adds time-limited rules on approved requests.")
Q(8,"You must scan VMs for vulnerabilities and exposed secrets without installing anything on them or affecting performance. What should you use?","Agentless scanning",["The Defender for Endpoint sensor only","Azure Machine Configuration","File integrity monitoring"],"Agentless scanning analyzes disk snapshots outside the VM.")
Q(8,"On-premises Windows servers must be protected by Defender for Servers and governed with Azure Policy. What must you do first?","Onboard the servers to Azure Arc",["Create an AWS connector","Deploy Azure Bastion","Enable Trusted launch"],"Arc makes the servers Azure resources so Defender and Policy can reach them.")
Q(8,"Compliance requires recording all administrator RDP sessions to VMs that have no public IP. Which Bastion SKU do you need?","Premium",["Developer","Basic","Standard"],"Session recording is a Premium feature.")
Q(8,"Which TWO features are part of Trusted launch?",["Secure Boot","vTPM"],["Just-in-time access","TLS inspection"],"Trusted launch combines Secure Boot, vTPM and boot integrity monitoring.")
YN(8,["Defender for Servers Plan 1 includes just-in-time VM access.","Azure Machine Configuration can apply to Arc-enabled servers.","Azure Disk Encryption is the recommended option for new VMs."],[0,1,0],"JIT is Plan 2. Machine Configuration covers Arc servers. ADE is retiring; use encryption at host.")
M(8,"Match each requirement to the feature.",[("Enforce a password policy inside the OS","Azure Machine Configuration"),("Detect changes to system files and registry","File integrity monitoring"),("Encrypt temp disks and caches end to end","Encryption at host"),("Block unsigned bootloaders","Secure Boot")],"In-guest policy, change detection, host encryption, boot trust.")
Q(8,"Which Defender for Servers plan do you need for file integrity monitoring and premium vulnerability management capabilities?","Plan 2",["Plan 1","Foundational CSPM","Either plan"],"Both are Plan 2 features.")
D(8,"Defender for Servers Plan 1","Defender for Servers Plan 2","Includes agentless scanning and JIT.",1,"Plan 1 is EDR-focused.")
D(8,"Azure Bastion","Just-in-time access","Opens an NSG rule for a limited time after a request.",1,"Bastion is the managed jump service.")
D(8,"Secure Boot","vTPM","Stores keys and measurements for attestation.",1,"Secure Boot verifies signatures at boot.")
D(8,"Azure Policy","Azure Machine Configuration","Audits settings inside the guest operating system.",1,"Plain Policy evaluates resource properties from outside.")
D(8,"Agent-based scanning","Agentless scanning","Works from disk snapshots.",1,"Agentless scanning never runs in the VM.")
